SERIALIZABLE SNAPSHOT ISOLATION (SSI) + 2PL + OCC COMPLETE NOTES (HINGLISH)

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
1. PROBLEM STATEMENT (WHY WE NEED THIS)
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Multiple transactions ek hi time pe database pe kaam karte hain

Goal:
- Data consistent rahe
- Performance fast rahe

Issue:
- Agar proper control nahi hua toh:
  Dirty Read
  Lost Update
  Write Skew
  Phantom Problems

Isliye hume concurrency control chahiye

Main approaches:
1. Pessimistic → 2PL
2. Optimistic → OCC / Snapshot Isolation / SSI

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
2. TWO PHASE LOCKING (2PL)
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Mindset:
"Mujhe lagta hai conflicts honge → pehle hi sab lock kar do"

Working:
- Phase 1: Locks acquire karo
- Phase 2: Locks release karo

Types:
- Shared lock (read)
- Exclusive lock (write)

Properties:
- Serializable
- Safe

Problems:
- Blocking hota hai
- Deadlocks ho sakte hain
- Performance slow ho jati hai

Real life:
Seat booking
Bank balance update
Inventory system

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
3. OPTIMISTIC CONCURRENCY CONTROL (OCC)
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Mindset:
"Mujhe lagta hai conflicts rare hain → freely kaam karo, end me check karo"

Steps:

1. Read Phase
- Snapshot se read karo
- No locks

2. Work Phase
- Changes local rakho

3. Validation Phase
- Check karo ki conflict hua ya nahi

4. Commit / Abort
- Valid → commit
- Conflict → rollback + retry

Advantage:
- High concurrency
- No blocking

Disadvantage:
- Retry karna pad sakta hai

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
4. SNAPSHOT ISOLATION (SI)
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Definition:
Snapshot = database ka ek fixed state at a given time

Transaction apne snapshot pe kaam karta hai
Even if database change ho jaye baad me

Example:
T1 snapshot me A = 100 dekhta hai
T2 update karke A = 50 kar deta hai
T1 ko fir bhi 100 hi dikhega

Properties:
- Readers writers ko block nahi karte
- Writers readers ko block nahi karte
- High performance

BUT:
Serializable guarantee nahi deta

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
5. DIRECT CONFLICT KYA HOTA HAI
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Conflict tab hota hai jab same data item pe clash ho

Types:

1. Write-Write conflict
T1 writes A
T2 writes A

2. Read-Write conflict
T1 reads A
T2 writes A before T1 commit

Agar alag-alag data items pe kaam ho raha hai
Toh direct conflict nahi hota

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
6. WRITE SKEW PROBLEM (MOST IMPORTANT)
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Example: Doctors On Call

Rule:
At least 1 doctor ON hona chahiye

Initial:
A = ON
B = ON

Transactions:

T1:
- Read B
- Write A = OFF

T2:
- Read A
- Write B = OFF

Observation:
T1 writes A
T2 writes B

Same data pe write nahi ho raha
Isliye:
No Write-Write conflict
No direct Read-Write conflict

Final state:
A = OFF
B = OFF

Rule break ho gaya

Key Insight:
Conflict data pe nahi, logic pe tha

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
7. ROOT CAUSE OF FAILURE
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Hidden dependency hai

T1 depends on B
T2 modifies B

T2 depends on A
T1 modifies A

Dependency graph:
T1 → T2
T2 → T1

Cycle present hai

Isko bolte hain:
Serialization cycle

Snapshot Isolation ye detect nahi karta
Isliye fail ho jata hai

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
8. SERIALIZABLE SNAPSHOT ISOLATION (SSI)
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Definition:
Snapshot Isolation + Dependency tracking

Goal:
Ensure serializability without heavy locking

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
9. SSI KA WORKING (STEP BY STEP)
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Step 1: Transactions start
T1 snapshot leta hai
T2 snapshot leta hai

Step 2: Reads track kiye jaate hain
T1 read → B
T2 read → A

Step 3: Writes hote hain
T1 write → A
T2 write → B

Step 4: Dependencies detect hoti hain

Case 1:
T1 ne B read kiya
T2 ne B write kiya
T1 → T2

Case 2:
T2 ne A read kiya
T1 ne A write kiya
T2 → T1

Step 5: Graph ban gaya
T1 → T2 → T1

Cycle detect ho gaya

Step 6: Abort
System ek transaction abort karega

Example:
T2 abort

Final:
A = OFF
B = ON

Rule satisfied

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
10. SSI KA CORE IDEA
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Snapshot Isolation:
Sirf data conflicts check karta hai

SSI:
Logical dependencies + cycles check karta hai

Golden line:
Conflict data pe nahi, dependency pe detect hota hai

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
11. DANGEROUS STRUCTURE
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Pattern:
T1 → T2 → T3

Agar ye chain complete ho gayi
Toh cycle ban sakta hai

SSI early abort kar deta hai
Taaki cycle na bane

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
12. 2PL VS SSI COMPARISON
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

2PL:
- Pessimistic
- Locks use karta hai
- Slow
- Deadlocks possible
- High contention systems ke liye best

SSI:
- Optimistic
- No heavy locks
- Fast
- No deadlocks
- Low contention systems ke liye best

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
13. KAB 2PL USE KARE
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Jab:
- Same data pe frequent writes ho
- Conflict chances high ho

Examples:
- Bank account updates
- Ticket booking (same seat)
- Inventory (last item)

Reason:
Retry expensive hota hai
Isliye lock better hai

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
14. KAB SSI USE KARE
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Jab:
- Read heavy system ho
- Conflict rare ho

Examples:
- Social media feeds
- E-commerce browsing
- Analytics dashboards

Reason:
High concurrency chahiye
Retry acceptable hai

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
15. REAL LIFE ANALOGY
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Library:

2PL:
Book pe lock laga diya
Jab tak return nahi hoti
Koi aur use nahi kar sakta

SSI:
Sabko book de di
End me check:
Agar clash hua
Toh kisi ek ko retry karna padega

Doctors case:

Without SSI:
A: B duty pe hai → main chhutti
B: A duty pe hai → main chhutti
Result: No doctor

With SSI:
System detect karta hai:
Dono ek dusre pe depend hain
Ek ko hi allow karega
Dusre ko abort karega

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
16. FINAL INTERVIEW SUMMARY
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

2PL:
Conflicts prevent karta hai using locks

SSI:
Conflicts detect karta hai using dependency graph

Snapshot Isolation:
Fast hai but not always correct

SSI:
Fast + Correct (Serializable)

Most Important Concept:
Write skew occurs when transactions update different rows but violate a global constraint, and SSI prevents it by detecting cycles in dependency graph

